-- R33 - EMAIL UNDER GMAIL'S CLIP: synthesis printed straight after the themes; HTML measured before sending and
-- trimmed to 95,000 bytes by moving detail to a Drive overflow file, never by dropping content or inputs.
-- Source: thread "Act on Neon feedback for Takeaways", 22 Nov 2026. The Fable email was 135 KB on 22 Nov (Gmail clips
-- at about 102 KB of HTML), and over the clip on 14, 15 and 16 Nov too.
-- Proposed 22 Nov 2026 and put in force the same morning with R32 (see R32_downgrade_primary_check.sql).
-- "revert R33" removes it. The call below is the exact call that was run.
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "The emailed digest stays under Gmail's clip: synthesis printed straight after the themes, HTML measured before sending and trimmed to 95,000 bytes without dropping content", "body": "EMAIL UNDER GMAIL'S CLIP (Fable emails of 14, 15, 16 and 22 Nov 2026 were 114 to 139 KB; Gmail hides everything after about 102 KB behind \"View entire message\", which cut the CROSS-THEME SYNTHESIS and the footer on his phone).\n\n1. PRINT ORDER. CROSS-THEME SYNTHESIS & HONEST CAVEATS prints straight after the last theme, before RADAR. It keeps its own heading. RADAR, LEDGER, ADMIN FLAGS and the FOOTER (its own FOOTER heading, QUESTION LIST block unchanged) follow, in that order.\n\n2. MEASURE. After assembly and before sending, measure the final HTML file in bytes with a script. Budget: 95,000 bytes.\n\n3. TRIM, in this order, stopping as soon as the file is under budget: (a) inline style attributes only where the colour key, a highlight or a table needs them; no style attribute on plain paragraphs, list items or cells (keep every style inline: the dashboard does not read a style block); (b) TESTED lines in the TRADE BOOK block: the first three, then the existing \"+ N more tested, in the file\" pointer; (c) LEDGER and RADAR one-liners with no highlight: at most 220 characters each, longer text moved whole to the Drive file named in (e); (d) EXTREME CHECK and FLOW CHECK paragraphs: at most 70 words each in the email, full text moved to that file; (e) the file is \"takeaways_overflow_<YYYY-MM-DD>\" in this pipeline's Drive folder, linked once in the footer. Never trimmed: the top line, THE LAST 24H IN 60 SECONDS, any trade card, any theme's My read & lean, the synthesis, any highlight, the QUESTION LIST block. Nothing is dropped: whatever leaves the email goes in the overflow file, and no input is read less.\n\n4. FOOTER line: \"Email: <KB> KB of 95 (trim steps: <letters or none>)\". Over budget after step 3: send anyway and print \"OVER CLIP\".", "rationale": "Gmail clips a message whose HTML passes about 102 KB. The Fable Takeaways sizes (Gmail sizeEstimate) were 138.5 KB on 14 Nov, 114.3 on 15, 118.2 on 16 and 135.1 on 22 Nov; 17, 19 and 21 Nov (90.3, 84.8, 105.6 with an 84 KB HTML part) were not clipped. On 22 Nov the HTML part was 113.7 KB with 17.7 KB of inline style attributes, and the last 12 KB (synthesis, admin flags, footer) fell below the clip. The prompt already says the clip must fall in the lower sections, but it put the synthesis, one of the most useful sections, there. Moving the synthesis up and trimming styling and overflow detail fixes it without dropping content or inputs. The prompt is at its byte cap, so the change goes in as a rule.", "evidence": "Gmail sizeEstimate of the Fable Macro Takeaways messages 14-22 Nov 2026; HTML section byte counts of the 22 Nov message (1a2006064e565f05) measured in the thread 'Act on Neon feedback for Takeaways'.", "revert_if": "Revert if the dashboard loses a section the feeder used to parse, or if an email under this rule still clips on three days.", "review_due": "2026-12-13", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
